findings.description:
The design adds reads of `config.json`, `.understandignore` and `meta.json`'s `analyzedFiles`. The only handling is one fallback, "[GAP: …] naming the unreadable file" (line 180), which does not distinguish:
- `config.json` present but not valid JSON;
- `.understandignore` absent, which is not the same as all-comments ("defaults only");
- `analyzedFiles` absent or non-numeric, which the reconciliation at lines 224–227 assumes away.

Hang, timeout and peer-disconnect are not addressed, even as not applicable to local reads. The gap-marker walkthrough (lines 406–411) covers only removing `meta.json`. The review standard requires an explicit handling strategy for each failure and at least one test asserting its observable signal. List absent, unreadable, malformed, empty and key-missing cases for each new read, with the gap text for each, and add walkthrough cases.
